1
00:00:00,250 --> 00:00:03,341
This dress sold MORE at $39 than at $34.

2
00:00:03,561 --> 00:00:06,559
Researchers at MIT and Chicago tested it.

3
00:00:06,629 --> 00:00:09,371
Same dress. Higher price. More sales.

4
00:00:09,641 --> 00:00:13,278
Why? Your brain reads prices from left to right, and it's lazy.

5
00:00:13,348 --> 00:00:15,649
It sees the nine first, and stops.

6
00:00:15,869 --> 00:00:19,030
So $9.99 feels like $9. Not $10.

7
00:00:19,300 --> 00:00:22,228
Psychologists call it the left-digit effect.

8
00:00:22,448 --> 00:00:25,226
That's why almost nothing costs a round number.

9
00:00:25,246 --> 00:00:28,673
$4.99. $19.99. $99.99.

10
00:00:28,943 --> 00:00:31,361
The fix? Round every price up in your head.

11
00:00:31,381 --> 00:00:34,100
$9.99 is $10. Always.

12
00:00:34,320 --> 00:00:37,736
So next time a price ends in 9, remember why…
